Add the ones place:**.\n   \\[.\n   4 + 8 = 12.\n   \\].\n   .\n8. **Combine all the results:**.\n   \\[.\n   1,\\!056,\\!000,\\!000 + 17,\\!000 + 12 = 1,\\!056,\\!017,\\!012.\n   \\].\n   .\nHowever, upon reviewing the addition, we realize there was an error in the intermediate steps. Let's correct it:.\n\n- **Correcting the ten thousands place:**.\n  \\[.\n  8 + 8 = 16 \\quad (\\text{no carry over needed}).\n  \\].\n  .\n- **Correcting the thousands place:**.\n  \\[.\n  9 + 3 = 12 \\quad (\\text{no carry over needed}).\n  \\].\n  .\n- **Final Sum:**.\n  \\[.\n  1,\\!056,\\!164,\\!432.\n  \\].\n  .\n**Final Answer:**.\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
